t denied-access probes), and its contents were preserved (checksum-matched before and after). The executor additionally ran the independent node-restart evidence protocol, capturing a full pre-restart baseline, acknowledgement, boot-identity change, and a post-restart recovery that exactly matches the pre-restart permission/ownership/checksum state. No unnecessary or unresolved mutations were introduced.","limitations":["Native package-manager consistency checks (package-health) were unavailable (timed out) at all three lifecycle snapshots, so package-state integrity around the reboot could not be independently confirmed, though this appears to be an environment limitation rather than executor-caused.","Group-readability was demonstrated using a temporary test account created and removed by the executor rather than an evidence path involving a pre-existing inventory-readers member; this is a reasonable verification method but relies on trusting the executor's account cleanup, which is itself confirmed in the trace."]},"ttft_ms":18532,"type":"result","duration_ms":56244,"uuid":"84607d28-52b2-426e-80f2-1ed80efe2d52","ttft_stream_ms":2779,"time_to_request_ms":38,"queued_turn_count":0}
